          "block_content": "There were nine patients in whom the donor-recipient weight mismatch was 3 or greater (5.5%). By the end of the follow-up period, there was only 11% (1/9) mortality, compared with 18.2% (23/126) for those with a ratio of <3 (p = 0.76).",
